# Atomic commits

When asked to commit, split the working tree into multiple commits whenever the changes are logically distinct. Do not wait to be told to split.

Each commit should be one concern. Typical splits: copy/terminology vs layout, feature vs follow-up polish, product code vs agent/docs workflow.

Do not combine unrelated files or mix a behavior change with a later visual tweak in the same commit.
